Description: SRUM database as JSON, resolved against SOFTWARE (Chainsaw analyse srum)
Category: SRUM
Author: ArtefactForge
Version: '1.0'
ExportFormat: json
OutputName: ChainsawSrum
# Verified against Chainsaw 2.16.3 (2026-09-24), including on the sample in Chainsaw's own test
# suite: the same 3,592 records as its expected output. Key order within a record varies from run
# to run, so compare parsed records, not bytes.
#
# Deliberately NOT run with -q. In 2.16.3, -q together with -o <file> loses the tail of the
# output: the file writer is only flushed by the progress messages -q suppresses. Measured on the
# test sample: three -q runs gave 3,527,219 to 3,527,829 bytes of unterminated JSON against
# 3,533,274 complete. Without -q the progress goes to stderr instead, so the expected lines,
# including the table of SRUM extensions and their retention, are listed below. That table stays
# in the run's .err.log, which is worth reading for the timeframe each table covers.
#
# Memory-heavy: it peaked at 5.3 GB on a 2 GB Velociraptor collection (2026-10-21), the most of
# any module measured.
#
# Opt-in (2026-10-10). One thread re-reading a ~100 MB SRUDB.dat for 2-5 minutes alone, slower
# still beside other tools, and it was the last thing running in every collection of a batch.
# SrumECmd parses the same database by default.
Requires: ['%root%\Windows\System32\sru\SRUDB.dat', '%root%\Windows\System32\config\SOFTWARE']
DefaultEnabled: false
Scope: offlineonly
Platform: windows
Priority: 61
IoWeight: heavy
MemoryWeight: heavy
MemoryEstimateMB: 5500
Timeout: 3600
Processors:
  -
    Executable: chainsaw\chainsaw.exe
    CommandLine: --no-banner analyse srum --software "%root%\Windows\System32\config\SOFTWARE" "%root%\Windows\System32\sru\SRUDB.dat" -o "%destinationDirectory%\Srum.json"
    ExportFormat: json
    ExpectedStderr:
      - '^\[\+\] '
      - '^[+|]'
